        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: कुंज",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कुंज — kuñj — \"a bower, a grove\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बगीचे के कोने में एक छोटा कुंज है। bagīce ke kone meṁ ek choṭā kuñj hai. There is a little bower in the corner of the garden."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "कुंज (kuñj) is a tatsama, Sanskrit kuñja, \"a place overrun with plants or creepers, a bower\" (Monier-Williams)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
